course: dictionary
lesson: 12184
title: Conditional: only if
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some things only happen when something else happens first. A word for this is conditional. «Your pocket money is conditional on doing your chores.» You get the money only if you do the chores first.
explain: Conditional sentences often use "if". «If it rains, we will stay in.» The rain is the condition, and staying in depends on it. The condition is what must happen first.
explain: In maths and computing, a conditional statement says "if this, then that". «If the light is green, then the robot moves forward.» The robot moves only when the condition is met.
fact: Conditional means depending on something else happening first.
fact: A condition is the thing that must happen first.
fact: «Conditional» is an adjective; «the conditional» is also a grammar name for sentences with "if".
fact: «If it rains, we will stay in» is a conditional sentence.
fact: Conditional on means "only if": «The trip is conditional on good weather.»
exercise: «The prize is conditional on finishing the race.» What does conditional mean here? | *Depending on finishing the race first | Painted gold for the winner | Given to everyone for free | Held in the park each year
exercise: «If it snows, the school will close.» Which part is the condition? | *If it snows | close | the school | the school will close
exercise: Which sentence is a conditional sentence? | Tidy rooms are nice. | *If you tidy your room, you can watch television. | You tidied your room yesterday. | The room is very tidy.
test: Ali says, «I will go to the park if the sun shines.» Which word shows the condition? | sun | go | park | *if
test: In a computer game, «If the player has a key, then the door opens.» What does this statement mean? | The player must find a door | The key opens every door | The door always opens | *The door opens only when the player has a key
exam: Which statement is conditional, saying "if this, then that"? | The bell is loud | We line up every morning | *If the bell rings, then we line up | Lining up is fun
